{% comment %}
  Wishlist page — the header's heart icon (sections/header.liquid) links
  here, but previously had nowhere to actually go; this section renders
  it. Wishlist data only ever lives in the browser's localStorage (see
  assets/wishlist.js), never on the server, so — same as
  recently-viewed-products.liquid — the actual product grid is entirely
  populated by JS after load, not server-rendered Liquid.

  Requires a Page in the Shopify admin with this section's template
  assigned (Page → Theme template → page.wishlist) — the same setup
  already needed for the About/FAQ/Contact pages elsewhere in this
  theme. The header links to /pages/wishlist by default.

  Pagination and filters reuse the exact markup/classes/CSS/JS
  (collection.css, collection.js's mobile filter-drawer logic) that
  sections/main-collection.liquid uses for the real catalog page —
  there's no Shopify collection or Search & Discovery filter object to
  drive this from server-side, since the product set here is an
  arbitrary, per-visitor localStorage list, so wishlist-page.js derives
  its own filter options (product type / vendor / price) from whatever
  products are actually in the wishlist and paginates client-side.
{% endcomment %}
{% # theme-check-disable AssetPreload %}
<link rel="preload" href="{{ 'collection.css' | asset_url }}" as="style" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet'">
<noscript>{{ 'collection.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}</noscript>
<link rel="preload" href="{{ 'wishlist-page.css' | asset_url }}" as="style" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet'">
<noscript>{{ 'wishlist-page.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}</noscript>
{% # theme-check-enable AssetPreload %}

{% render 'breadcrumbs' %}

<div class="full-width j-page-hero-band">
  <div class="j-page-hero-band__inner">
    <div class="j-section-title">
      <h1>{{ page.title | default: 'Wishlist' }}</h1>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="j-collection j-wishlist-page">
  <div class="page-width">

    <div class="j-collection-layout">

      <aside class="j-collection-sidebar" id="CollectionFilters">
        <div class="j-collection-filters" id="WishlistFiltersPanel"></div>
      </aside>

      <div class="j-filter-overlay"></div>

      <div class="j-collection-content">

        <div class="j-collection-toolbar">
          <button
            type="button"
            class="j-filter-toggle"
            id="WishlistFilterToggle"
            aria-expanded="false"
            aria-controls="CollectionFilters"
            hidden
          >
            <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M3 5h14M6 10h8M8.5 15h3" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round"/>
            </svg>
            {{ 'filters.title' | t }}
          </button>

          <form id="WishlistSortForm">
            <label for="WishlistSortBy">
              {{ 'collection.sort_by' | t }}
            </label>

            <div class="j-collection-sort">
              <select id="WishlistSortBy" name="sort_by">
                <option value="featured">{{ 'collection.sort_featured' | t }}</option>
                <option value="price-ascending">{{ 'collection.sort_price_ascending' | t }}</option>
                <option value="price-descending">{{ 'collection.sort_price_descending' | t }}</option>
                <option value="title-ascending">{{ 'collection.sort_title_ascending' | t }}</option>
                <option value="title-descending">{{ 'collection.sort_title_descending' | t }}</option>
              </select>

              <svg class="j-collection-sort__icon" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M5 7.5 10 12.5 15 7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </div>
          </form>
        </div>

        {% comment %}
          Wishlist data only ever lives in localStorage, so there's
          nothing for Liquid to render server-side here — the grid was
          simply empty until wishlist-page.js's fetches resolved, which
          on a slow connection or a longer wishlist reads as the page
          being broken (blank grid, no products, no empty-state message
          either) for however long that takes. These skeleton cards fill
          that gap with an obviously-loading placeholder instead;
          wishlist-page.js replaces this element's entire contents with
          the real cards (or the empty state) the moment it has an
          answer, so they never linger alongside real content.
        {% endcomment %}
        <div class="j-collection-grid" id="WishlistPageProducts">
          {% render 'product-grid-skeleton', count: 4 %}
        </div>

        {% comment %}
          Shown by wishlist-page.js only once it's actually confirmed the
          wishlist is empty (no stored handles, every stored product has
          since been deleted, or the active filters match nothing) —
          hidden by default so it doesn't flash before JS has had a
          chance to check, matching the same empty/no-JS-safe pattern
          used elsewhere (e.g. the cart drawer's empty state).
        {% endcomment %}
        <div class="j-wishlist-page__empty" id="WishlistPageEmpty" hidden>
          <div class="j-wishlist-page__empty-icon">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M12 20.5s-7.5-4.6-9.7-9.1C.7 7.7 2.6 4 6.3 4c2 0 3.8 1 4.9 2.6C12.3 5 14.1 4 16.1 4c3.7 0 5.6 3.7 4 7.4-2.2 4.5-9.7 9.1-9.7 9.1Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p id="WishlistPageEmptyText">{{ 'product.wishlist_empty' | t }}</p>
          <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}" class="j-button j-wishlist-page__continue">
            {{ 'cart.continue_shopping' | t }}
          </a>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<script src="{{ 'collection.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
<script src="{{ 'wishlist-page.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Wishlist page",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
